# TEMPLATE. Copy to the project root as .cursorrules, or paste into Cursor's
# global rules. Replace <BRAIN> with the absolute path to this repo, e.g.
# C:\Users\<me>\engineering-brain — then delete these three lines.

My engineering knowledge base is at <BRAIN>. It is the source of truth for how I
work. Read it before writing code, running commands, or answering technical
questions.

Start with <BRAIN>/INDEX.md — it gives the read order for the files in
<BRAIN>/knowledge/. Read those files directly rather than working from memory of
them. If you can only read one, read <BRAIN>/knowledge/20-method.md: it has my
debugging method and my rules about changing data.

Before you touch anything, tell me in a few lines what you took away — the
debugging method and what I want escalated rather than guessed.

This file is a pointer, not a copy. Do not restate the knowledge base here.

When I say "add that to the brain": append one dated, generalised line to
<BRAIN>/INBOX.md and stop there. Do not edit <BRAIN>/knowledge/ from here —
promotion out of the inbox happens in a separate review pass. Strip company
specifics on the way in: no table or DAG names, hosts, tickets, or people.

Project-specific rules can go below this line.
